<h1>Working with an AI agent</h1>
<p>Reliaburger is an orchestrator.
Its CLI is <code>relish</code>.</p>
<p>Intro paragraph.</p>
<aside class="agents-install" id="add-to-your-agent" aria-labelledby="add-to-your-agent-title">
<h2 id="add-to-your-agent-title">Add it to your agent <a class="permalink" href="#add-to-your-agent" aria-label="Link to the install buttons">#</a></h2>
<p>Each button adds one MCP server, <code>reliaburger</code>, that runs <code>relish mcp</code>: read-only tools over stdio, with no port, no trust flag and no auto-approval. Your client shows the entry and asks before it adds it. Install <code>relish</code> 0.2.7 or later first (<code>relish agent version</code> says which you have); the server runs the <code>relish</code> on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
<p class="agents-install-buttons"><a class="install-button" href="cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install?name=reliaburger&amp;config=eyJhcmdzIjpbIm1jcCJdLCJjb21tYW5kIjoicmVsaXNoIn0%3D">Add to Cursor</a><a class="install-button" href="vscode:mcp/install?%7B%22args%22%3A%5B%22mcp%22%5D%2C%22command%22%3A%22relish%22%2C%22name%22%3A%22reliaburger%22%7D">Add to VS Code</a><a class="install-button" href="goose://extension?cmd=relish&amp;arg=mcp&amp;id=reliaburger&amp;name=Reliaburger&amp;description=Reliaburger%3A%20read-only%20cluster%20status%2C%20diagnosis%20and%20logs">Add to Goose</a></p>
<p>Claude Code, from a shell:</p>
<pre><code data-install-command>claude mcp add reliaburger -- relish mcp</code></pre>
<p>Or let <code>relish agent setup</code> find every agent on this machine and show the change before it writes anything (see <a href="#wiring-up-your-agent">Wiring up your agent</a>). Give the server a read-only token: see <a href="#a-read-only-token">A read-only token</a>.</p>
</aside>
